-- title:
--   Constructing post-ledger bridge inputs with preselected margins
-- statement:
--   Fix $c>C_0$, $W>0$, a positive regular mesh, guarded tail family $F$, and a fixed-rich-source witness $X$. Let $c_s>0$, an exponent $E>0$, and positive $C_f,m$ be selected before the mesh. Require $2\sum_{p\le W}b_p\le E(c_s/4)$, where $b_p$ are the prescribed head upper coefficients, and require $m$ equal the prescribed head-margin formula from $E$, the head linear floors, and $C_f$. Suppose the scalar families $m_f,\ell_Y,\Lambda_0$ eventually equal the witness frozen mass, logarithmic target, and rounded scalar. Let $q_f,a_f$ be the final active mass and height built from these families and the common extended guarded base mass. Suppose eventually $(c_s/4)N\le q_f$, $|q_f|\le C_f|N|$, and $a_f/q_f$ lies between the fixed physical log endpoints with half the prescribed physical margin on each side. Then eventually each source index has compatible head reserve, physical interpolation target, and post-height bridge inputs $J$. They retain the source target and its source-cell margin, exponent $E$, the literal selector-tail head factorizations, the base mass as both $J.\widetilde q$ and the reserve active mass, and the prescribed family values for $d,q_0,A_0,q_n$. In particular,
--
--   $$J.\mathrm{targetInputs.headMargin}=m,\qquad J.\mathrm{targetInputs.physicalEta}=\tfrac12\eta_{\rm fixed}.$$
--
--   The final-mass upper constant and head margin remain those selected before the final mesh.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/ShouqiaoW/erdos/blob/61325b10bbdc29f4fb5e0618b414b9f2189333ad/390/lean/Erdos390/WholePaper/BankPaperCanonicalSectionNinePostHeightSourceFirstPreselectedPostLedgerConnector.lean#L35-L472

